First describe the image: In the figure there are six marked points: the top is A, the upper left is Zoo, the upper right is Port, the lower left is B, the lower middle is Park, and the lower right is C. The visible roads form four small loops: the upper loop A-Zoo-Port-A; the lower-left loop B-Park-Zoo-B; the lower-right loop C-Port-Park-C; and the central triangular loop Zoo-Park-Port-Zoo.

Then reason: Let the lengths of the visible road segments be represented by their names. According to the problem statement and the loops in the figure:
A-Zoo + Zoo-Port + Port-A = 10;
B-Park + Park-Zoo + Zoo-B = 12;
C-Port + Port-Park + Park-C = 13;
Zoo-Park + Park-Port + Port-Zoo = 15.
Add the first three station loops, obtaining 10 + 12 + 13 = 35. This total includes the outer route A-Zoo-B-Park-C-Port-A once, and also includes the central triangle Zoo-Park-Port-Zoo once. The length of the central triangle is known to be 15, so the required length of the outer route is 35 - 15 = 20 km.

